// §14 entry 11 -- capability stored in module-level mutable state ->
// EXS-E0501.
//
// §4.1 rule 7: "No module-level mutable state. (EXS-E0500; with a
// capability, EXS-E0501.)" A capability held at module scope is reachable
// from anywhere in the module with no caller in the chain having to grant
// it -- exactly the ambient-authority class §4 exists to make
// unrepresentable (§2.4: "Ambient authority | §4 capability model |
// EXS-E0421, E0500, E0501, E0510").
//
// `rete` has no literal, no cast and no default (§4.1 rule 1: "Capability
// types are unforgeable"), so this binding cannot be given an initial
// value at all -- which is not a reason to accept the declaration; the
// VIOLATION is the module-level `mutabilis` binding of capability type
// existing, independent of what (if anything) could ever initialize it.

mutabilis retis_globalis: rete

